The sysroot generator (Linker/Sysroot/, Scripts/ship_sysroot_inputs.py and
related maintainer scripts) follows designs from the Zig project
(https://ziglang.org, https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig): glibc stub shared
objects generated from abilist data with version gating, the
majority-vote deduplication of per-target libc headers into a generic tree
plus per-target overrides, and libc start files compiled from a shipped
source subset. No Zig code or data is included.

Apple's SDK and Microsoft's MSVC / Windows SDK are never distributed with
Kairo. Sysroots built from them on your machine (scripts/) stay subject to
their own license terms.

scripts/msvc-sysroot can build a windows-msvc sysroot on your machine. After
you accept Microsoft's license it downloads the xwin tool (MIT OR Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/Jake-Shadle/xwin; pinned to 0.10.0 and checked against a
sha256), and xwin downloads Microsoft's MSVC CRT and Windows SDK packages.
Neither xwin nor those packages is distributed with Kairo.
